{"title":"Real axis","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_axis&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The real <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Axis\" title=\"Axis\">axis</a> in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_plane\" title=\"Complex plane\">complex plane</a> roughly corresponds to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=X-axis\" title=\"X-axis\">x-axis</a> on the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cartesian_plane\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cartesian plane\">Cartesian plane</a>.\nIt is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_axis\" title=\"Imaginary axis\">imaginary axis</a> and intersects at 0.\nEach <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Unit\" title=\"Unit\">unit</a> has a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Length\" title=\"Length\">length</a> of 1 and the numbers on this line are \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/858dd485d2edcd003e727e333e5a372ea1ce943c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ldots-2,-1,0,1,2\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Points that are on the real axis have no imaginary part.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Real_axis&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018104829\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 11/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 268/209